From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a shader effect's arrays reach it while its filter
 animates

An array the shell set with updateShaderEffect() reached viz under a
compositor animation of the element's filter only when something else
rebuilt the compositor's property trees. The cloth close effect sets its
points every frame under a compositor-run fade, so it drew the window
flat and only faded it.

Setting an array rebuilds the element's filters with it, and
EffectPaintPropertyNode::State::ComputeChange calls any filter change a
composited value while a filter animation runs on the compositor. A
composited value schedules no PaintArtifactCompositor update, and Blink
has no direct update for filters, so the cc effect node kept its old
arrays until an unrelated full update wrote the node again.

- A change to a shader effect's arrays under a running filter or
  backdrop filter animation is a simple value.
- PaintPropertyTreeBuilder writes a simple shader array change straight
  to the cc effect node (PropertyTreeManager::DirectlyUpdateShaderArrays)
  and commits, as it does opacity. The node keeps its filter values,
  which the animation owns, and the animation keeps the arrays (patch
  0274's EffectTree::OnFilterAnimated).
- If the node cannot be found, the change makes a full update, which
  writes the arrays too.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine job builds it on `crux`.
